# BGA Full-Stack Topology Progress

## Context

- Date: 2026-06-14T07:19:08+05:30
- Main branch: `0hmx/better-bga`
- Main HEAD: `a6bbb2eb`
- Task worktree: `.claude/worktrees/bga-full-stack`
- Task branch: `codex/bga-full-stack`
- Sub-agent: `Pauli` (`019ec3d0-8682-70e0-9c28-77a8a4167843`)

## Goal

Remove the BGA topology generator's hard-coded two-layer model and make BGA multilayer mesh nodes span the full board stack from top through bottom.

## Findings

- `lib/solvers/BgaTopologyGeneratorSolver/BgaTopologyGeneratorSolver.ts` hard-codes `static readonly layerCount = 2`.
- The obstacle merge stage trims only `z > 0`, which collapses every non-top layer into one semantic bucket.
- Replacement obstacle nodes are inserted only for `z > 0`, so top-layer ignored obstacles are effectively invisible to the BGA-local topology.
- `mergeOverlappingObstacles` remaps merged obstacle layers to only `top` / `bottom`.
- Current tests explicitly encode the broken contract with a fixed two-layer expectation.

## Baseline

- `bun test tests/component-detection-bga-only.test.ts -t "BGA topology generator"`
- Result before edits: 3 passing tests, 0 failing tests

## Completed

1. Replaced static BGA layer count usage with the input SRJ layer count.
2. Made ignored-obstacle trimming and replacement respect exact blocked z sets, including top/internal/bottom occupancy.
3. Updated merged ignored-obstacle metadata so arbitrary stack-layer occupancy is preserved.
4. Flattened BGA component-node remapping so real `availableZ` subsets survive topology-planning merge.
5. Fixed BGA expansion collision handling so single-layer expansion nodes cannot grow into multilayer replacement obstacles.
6. Rewrote the BGA tests around full-stack behavior and exact-layer replacement semantics.

## Verification

- `bun test tests/component-detection-bga-only.test.ts`
- `bun test tests/repro/srj18-sample013-component-topology-connectivity.test.ts`
- Result after edits: passing

## Residual Risk

- Some downstream code outside the BGA topology path still uses `availableZ[0]` as a representative layer for multilayer nodes. The verified repros pass, but this remains the main area to watch in future routing cases.

